    <tags>porta ports localhost developer-tools network process tray utility</tags>
    <summary>See what is listening on your ports, from the tray, and stop it</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
A door in the notification area that lists every program listening on a
network port.

* The port, the process, what it was started with, and how long it has run.
* Marks ports reachable from the network, not just from this machine.
* Open one in the browser, or stop the process, from the menu.
* Hides Windows' own services unless you ask for them.

For "port 3000 is already in use" and "which forgotten dev server is this?".
A single small executable with no runtime dependencies.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/kidchenko/porta/releases</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
